  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 28f310e05cc019a48855581da30b411e, type: 3}
  m_Name: SisigHistory
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lines:
  - text: 'Listen for that sizzle! We''re heading to Pampanga to discover one of
      its most famous dishes: sisig!'
    characterSprite: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Let me tell you the history and origin of pampanga sisig.
    characterSprite: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Sisig has roots in Kapampangan food culture.
    characterSprite: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Historical records from the 18th century describe an older sour preparation
      made with fruits like green papaya or guava.
    characterSprite: {fileID: 0}
  - text: The modern chopped-pork version became famous,
    characterSprite: {fileID: 0}
  - text: "in Angeles City during the 1970s, particularly through Lucia \u201CAling
      Lucing\u201D Cunanan."
    characterSprite: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Today, sisig commonly features chopped grilled pork, onions, calamansi,
      chili, and seasonings.
    characterSprite: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Its smoky and tangy flavors have helped make it a Filipino favorite.
    characterSprite: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Did you know?
    characterSprite: {fileID: -8056027616224820867, guid: 783feefcd5809a142b7b39ffbbe1c917, type: 3}
  - text: Sisig wasn't always a sizzling pork dish! Its older form was a sour preparation,
      showing how recipes can change over generations.
    characterSprite: {fileID: 0}
